.TH HD-CONFIG-REMOVE 1 "October 2026" "hd-base" "HyprDebian"
.SH NAME
hd-config-remove \- remove keys from the hyprdebian configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hd-config-remove
.I key
.RI [ key ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hd-config-remove
removes each
.I key
and its value from the JSON object of the configuration.
Only keys of that object itself are removed; it does not reach into the
values.
The other keys stay as they are.
See
.BR hd-config (7)
for how the configuration is used.
.PP
Who runs it decides which configuration it changes.
Run as root, it is the configuration of the system,
.IR /etc/hyprdebian/config.json ;
run as any other user, it is the configuration of that user,
.IR ~/.config/hyprdebian/config.json .
.PP
A key that is not in the configuration is skipped, and when the configuration does not exist, nothing is done.
Neither is an error, so a package can remove its keys whether or not it ever
set them.
When none of the keys is there, the file is not written.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ,\  \-\-help
Show a short help and exit.
.TP
.I key
A key to remove. May be given more than once.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when the keys are no longer in the configuration, 1 on an error, 2 on
wrong arguments.
On an error the file is left as it was.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hyprdebian/config.json
The configuration of the system, which root changes.
.TP
.I ~/.config/hyprdebian/config.json
The configuration of a user, which that user changes.
.SH EXAMPLES
Remove the settings of hd-example:
.PP
.RS
hd-config-remove hd-example
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hd-config (7),
.BR hd-config-update (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
